+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report — `hickory-proto`
+
+Fifteen hegel property tests were added inside the existing unit-test modules of
+`crates/proto/src/rr/domain/name.rs`, `crates/proto/src/rr/domain/label.rs`,
+`crates/proto/src/op/message.rs`, and `crates/proto/src/rr/serial_number.rs`
+(dev-dependency: `hegeltest = "0.28.2"`).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+| # | Property | Test name | Evidence |
+|---|----------|-----------|----------|
+| 1 | A `Name` emitted to wire format decodes back to the same name (case-sensitively; wire names are always FQDN) | `hegel_name_wire_roundtrip` (name.rs) | Existing `test_read`/`test_write_to` fixed examples; `Name::encoded_len` doc says `is_fqdn` is ignored on the wire |
+| 2 | Many names (frequently sharing suffixes) emitted through one encoder — exercising name compression — decode back in order, byte-for-byte including case | `hegel_name_compression_roundtrip` (name.rs) | Existing `test_pointer*` tests; `BinEncoder::get_label_pointer` matches byte-exactly |
+| 3 | `Name::read` never panics on arbitrary bytes (biased toward pointer/label markers) | `hegel_name_read_never_panics` (name.rs) | `fuzz/fuzz_targets/*`; existing `test_recursive_pointer`, `test_bin_overlap_enforced` |
+| 4 | `Name::from_ascii` parses `Name::to_ascii` output back to the same name, for arbitrary raw-byte labels | `hegel_name_to_ascii_from_ascii_roundtrip` (name.rs) — **FAILING, suspected bug** | `from_ascii` doc examples parse `\056`-style escapes; `to_utf8` doc: output "could be used with parse"; RFC 1035 §5.1 escaping exists to make this reversible |
+| 5 | Same round-trip restricted to the label alphabet `from_ascii` accepts unescaped, plus embedded dots (`\.` escape) | `hegel_name_to_ascii_from_ascii_roundtrip_safe_labels` (name.rs) | Same as #4; pins the working subset |
+| 6 | `Name::cmp` agrees with an independently implemented RFC 4034 §6.1 canonical-order reference (labels compared right-to-left, lowercased, plus the relative-before-FQDN rule) | `hegel_name_cmp_matches_rfc4034_reference` (name.rs) | RFC text quoted on `Ord for Name`; existing `test_partial_cmp` |
